    - The blindfold animation is being changed to the parent container, which will slide in from the top and then slide up from the bottom on hide.
    - Child content should be active = "true" _before_ the animation is run on the parent container: that single call will properly animate the child contents

    BLINDFOLD DEFAULTS:ks
    - playerHud_overlay_blindfold_@@color@@: active = "false"
    - overlay_blindfold_##_@@color@@: active = "false"
    - overlay_district_card_display_@@color@@: active = "false", color = "clear", image = ""
    - overlay_site_card_display_@@color@@: active = "false", color = "clear", image = ""

    BLINDFOLD ACTIVATION PROCEDURE:
    - randomly select one of the overlay_blindfold_##_@@color@@ images to reveal, set it to active = "true"
    - if there is a location set, set the district and site cards attributes as follows, in one UI.setAttributes call for each:
      - {active = "true", color = "White", image = "<corresponding district/site image>"}
    - call UI.show() on playerHud_overlay_blindfold_@@color@@

    BLINDFOLD DEACTIVATION PROCEDURE:
    - inside a U.chain call:
      - function #1: call UI.hide() on playerHud_overlay_blindfold_@@color@@, return a 3-second wait
      - function #2: restore defaults to CHILD elements only: set overlay_blindfold_##_@@color@@ to active = "false", set the district and site card attributes as follows, in one UI.setAttributes call for each:
        - {active = "false", color = "clear", image = ""}


